Lagging cluster replica read permanently drops live entry from index
On a redis_cluster2 filer with useReadOnly or routeByLatency enabled, a file that was just created can vanish from directory listings for good while its metadata and data still exist: it stays readable by exact path but is no longer listed, and a later recursive delete of the parent will skip it. Before this change a stale replica read only skipped the entry for that one listing; now the listing acts on it with a ZREM that goes to the master, and the safety re-check (EXISTS) is itself a read-only command routed to the same lagging replica, so it confirms the stale answer and the member is never restored. Running the confirmation against the slot master (go-redis ClusterClient.MasterForKey), or skipping the cleanup when replica reads are enabled, keeps the destructive decision off stale data.
